From: OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex (GPT-5) <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: as21xxx: add config_init firmware readiness fallback

The BPI-R4 Pro 8X vendor AS21xxx driver does not assume that a PHY
which reached probe will remain IPC-ready for later phylib init.  Its
config_init path polls firmware version through IPC and reloads the
AS21xxx firmware if the firmware does not answer.

That protects against reset/order cases that happen after initial MDIO
enumeration: the MDIO device may still exist, but the embedded firmware
may not yet be alive, may have restarted, or may have lost IPC parity
state before phylib configures the link.

Adapt the same runtime guard to the current 6.12 AS21xxx driver without
copying the vendor debugfs or board-specific LED policy.  Sync IPC
parity, poll firmware version for the existing two-second IPC budget, and
retry firmware load once when the firmware does not answer.  Re-enable
PTP clock and USXGMII DPC RA after the guard, matching the probe-time
runtime setup already present in this driver.

This is a second-layer guard.  It does not replace the firmware-loader
busy retry used during DT firmware load; it handles the later
config_init/readiness case once the concrete AS21xxx driver is already
bound.

Behavior source: Banana Pi BPI-R4 Pro 8X vendor as21xxx.c
as21xxx_config_init() / aeon_wait_reset_complete() behavior, adapted for
the current ImmortalWrt 25.12 Linux 6.12 AS21xxx driver organization.

Adapted-by: OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex (GPT-5)
---
 drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c | 64 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 64 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <linux/bitfield.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/firmware.h>
+#include <linux/iopoll.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/phy.h>
@@ -702,6 +703,53 @@
 				 sizeof(data), NULL);
 }
 
+static int aeon_wait_reset_complete(struct phy_device *phydev)
+{
+	struct as21xxx_priv *priv = phydev->priv;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = aeon_ipc_sync_parity(phydev, priv);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	return read_poll_timeout(aeon_ipc_get_fw_version, ret,
+				 ret == 0, AEON_IPC_DELAY,
+				 AEON_IPC_TIMEOUT, false, phydev);
+}
+
+static int as21xxx_config_init(struct phy_device *phydev)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = aeon_wait_reset_complete(phydev);
+	if (ret) {
+		phydev_warn(phydev,
+			    "firmware IPC not ready during config_init, reloading\n");
+
+		ret = aeon_firmware_load_wait(phydev);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+
+		ret = aeon_wait_reset_complete(phydev);
+		if (ret) {
+			phydev_err(phydev,
+				   "firmware IPC still not ready after reload: %d\n",
+				   ret);
+			return -ENODEV;
+		}
+	}
+
+	ret = phy_set_bits_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1, VEND1_PTP_CLK,
+			       VEND1_PTP_CLK_EN);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	if (phydev->interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII)
+		ret = aeon_dpc_ra_enable(phydev);
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
 static int as21xxx_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
 	struct as21xxx_priv *priv;
@@ -1200,6 +1248,7 @@
 		.match_phy_device = as21xxx_match_phy_device,
 		.read_status	= as21xxx_read_status,
 		.get_features	= as21xxx_get_features,
+		.config_init	= as21xxx_config_init,
 		.read_mmd	= as21xxx_read_mmd,
 		.led_brightness_set = as21xxx_led_brightness_set,
 		.led_hw_is_supported = as21xxx_led_hw_is_supported,
